"Wmatrix corpus analysis of UK General Election Manifestos (https://ucrel.lancs.ac.uk/wmatrix/ukmanifestos2024/)\nciteturn22view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ucrel.lancs.ac.uk/wmatrix/ukmanifestos2024/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 97\nL0: # Wmatrix corpus analysis of UK General Election Manifestos\nL1: #### Analysis of earlier UK General Election Manifestos\nL2: The 2005 UK General Election Manifestos were analysed in the online tutorials for Wmatrix showing the 【0†comparison of the Liberal Democrats and Labour Party Manifestos】. Further examples of the application to the 2010 general election manifestos can be seen on 【1†my blog†twibmr.blogspot.com】. The 【2†plain text versions of the 2010 UK election manifestos】 can be downloaded for use in your favourite text analysis software (with thanks to Martin Wynne for editing two of the files).\nL3: 【3†TEI encoded versions of the 2010 election manifestos】 are now available (with thanks to Lou Burnard). The analysis of seven manifestos for 【4†2015】, 【5†2017】, and 【6†2019】 are also available. The recent manifesto files are also available on 【7†GitHub†github.com】.\nL4: #### Analysis of 2024 UK General Election Manifestos\nL5: \nL6: In the following table, each manifesto will be presented along with a set of corpus analyses.\nL7: \nL8: In addition, when all the manifestos are published you will be able to download crosstabs of 【8†word】, 【9†POS】 and 【10†semantic tag】 frequencies with log-likelihood and dispersion statistics. These are tab delimited so can be opened in your favourite spreadsheet application.\nL9:  | Conservatives  | Labour  | Liberal Democrats  | Green Party  | Plaid Cymru  | Scottish National Party  | Reform UK\nL10: Party website  | 【11†www.conservatives.com†www.conservatives.com】  | 【12†labour.org.uk†labour.org.uk】  | 【13†www.libdems.org.uk†www.libdems.org.uk】  | 【14†greenparty.org.uk†greenparty.org.uk】  | 【15†www.plaid.cymru†www.plaid.cymru】  | 【16†www.snp.org†www.snp.org】  | 【17†www.reformparty.uk†www.reformparty.uk】\nL11: Launch date  | 11 June 2024  | 13 June 2024  | 10 June 2024  | 12 June 2024  | 13 June 2024  | 19 June 2024  | 17 June 2024\nL12: Direct link  | 【18†PDF†public.conservatives.com】  | 【19†PDF†labour.org.uk】  | 【20†PDF†www.libdems.org.uk】  | 【21†PDF†greenparty.org.uk】  | 【22†PDF†assets.nationbuilder.com】  | 【23†PDF†s3-eu-west-2.amazonaws.com】  | 【24†PDF†assets.nationbuilder.com】\nL13: Local copy  | 【25†PDF】  | 【26†PDF】  | 【27†PDF】  | 【28†PDF】  | 【29†PDF】  | 【30†PDF】  | 【31†PDF】\nL14: Edited text version  | 【32†TXT】  | 【33†TXT】  | 【34†TXT】  | 【35†TXT】  | 【36†TXT】  | 【37†TXT】  | 【38†TXT】\nL15: Number of words (tokens)  | 25,305  | 23,809  | 21,366  | 19,009  | 16,639  | 7,776  | 6,701\nL16: Number of unique words (types)  | 4,469  | 4,078  | 3,924  | 3,646  | 3,255  | 1,832  | 1,869\nL17: Word frequency list  | 【39†TXT】  | 【40†TXT】  | 【41†TXT】  | 【42†TXT】  | 【43†TXT】  | 【44†TXT】  | 【45†TXT】\nL18: Key word cloud  | 【46†Figure 1】  | 【47†Figure 3】  | 【48†Figure 5】  | 【49†Figure 7】  | 【50†Figure 9】  | 【51†Figure 11】  | 【52†Figure 13】\nL19: Key semantic tag cloud  | 【53†Figure 2】  | 【54†Figure 4】  | 【55†Figure 6】  | 【56†Figure 8】  | 【57†Figure 10】  | 【58†Figure 12】  | 【59†Figure 14】\nL20: As in previous elections, I will make local copies of manifestos available since they often disappear offline after the election. To prepare the text versions, I will use Adobe Reader to save as text and then manually edit (using 【60†VS Code†code.visualstudio.com】) a small number of items such as headers, footers and page numbers to store them in pseudo-XML-style tags.\nL21: In addition, I will follow the 【61†input format guidelines for CLAWS】 and convert n-dashes, pound signs, begin and end quotes to XML entities.\nL22: Notes:\nL23: 1. The choice of which parties to cover is again based on those appearing in the BBC 【62†election debates†www.bbc.co.uk】 and 【63†Newscast†www.bbc.co.uk】 leaders and manifesto coverage.\nL24: 2. For Labour, I used the 【64†large print PDF version†labour.org.uk】 (【65†local copy PDF】) because the standard PDF couldn't be converted to txt by Adobe Acrobat Reader\nL25: A note on word counts: Wmatrix counts semantically meaningful multiword expressions (MWEs) as one item, so other corpus software may well provide different counts here. These figures also depend on tokenisation in our NLP pipeline (by CLAWS).\nL26: \nL27: Word frequency lists are tab delimited so you can load them in to your favourite spreadsheet program. MWEs are shown in the word frequency lists as words connected by underscore characters.\nL28: Key word and semantic tag clouds are produced by comparing the data with the BNC Written Sampler corpus. The larger the font, the higher the log-likelihood score, so larger items are more significantly overused compared to the reference corpus. See the 【66†Wmatrix main page】 and 【0†online tutorials】 if you want more details about how this works.\nL29: \nL30: * * *\nL31: \nL32: 【67†Image】\nL33: Figure 1: Conservatives Key Word Cloud\nL34: \nL35: * * *\nL36: \nL37: 【68†Image】\nL38: Figure 2: Conservatives Key Semantic Tag Cloud\nL39: \nL40: * * *\nL41: 【69†Image】\nL42: Figure 3: Labour Key Word Cloud\nL43: \nL44: * * *\nL45: \nL46: 【70†Image】\nL47: Figure 4: Labour Key Semantic Tag Cloud\nL48: \nL49: * * *\nL50: \nL51: 【71†Image】\nL52: Figure 5: Liberal Democrats Key Word Cloud\nL53: \nL54: * * *\nL55: \nL56: 【72†Image】\nL57: Figure 6: Liberal Democrats Key Semantic Tag Cloud\nL58: \nL59: * * *\nL60: \nL61: 【73†Image】\nL62: Figure 7: Green Key Word Cloud\nL63: \nL64: * * *\nL65: \nL66: 【74†Image】\nL67: Figure 8: Green Key Semantic Tag Cloud\nL68: \nL69: * * *\nL70: \nL71: 【75†Image】\nL72: Figure 9: Plaid Cymru Key Word Cloud\nL73: \nL74: * * *\nL75: \nL76: 【76†Image】\nL77: Figure 10: Plaid Cymru Key Semantic Tag Cloud\nL78: \nL79: * * *\nL80: 【77†Image】\nL81: Figure 11: SNP Key Word Cloud\nL82: \nL83: * * *\nL84: \nL85: 【78†Image】\nL86: Figure 12: SNP Key Semantic Tag Cloud\nL87: \nL88: * * *\nL89: \nL90: 【79†Image】\nL91: Figure 13: Reform UK Party Key Word Cloud\nL92: \nL93: * * *\nL94: \nL95: 【80†Image】\nL96: Figure 14: Reform UK Party Key Semantic Tag Cloud\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2024 Manifestos - The Party of Wales (https://www.partyof.wales/2024)\nciteturn22view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.partyof.wales/2024\",\"lineno\":18}); Total lines: 71\nL0: 【0†Image†www.facebook.com】\nL1: \nL2:   * 【1†About】\nL3:     * 【2†Leader】\nL4:     * 【3†Elected Members】\nL5:     * 【4†National Sections】\nL6:     * 【5†Governance】\nL7:     * 【6†Work for us】\nL8:     * 【7†Contact】\nL9:   * 【8†Get involved】\nL10:     * 【9†Volunteer】\nL11:     * 【10†Donate】\nL12:     * 【11†Support】\nL13:       * 【12†Clwb 500】\nL14:       * 【13†Wills and Legacies】\nL15:     * 【14†Join】\nL16:     * 【15†Events】\nL17:       * 【16†Events】\nL18:       * 【17†Conference】\nL19:   *   * # 2024 Manifestos\nL20: ### Westminster Election\nL21: \nL22: 【18†2024 Manifesto (.pdf)†assets.nationbuilder.com】\nL23: \nL24: 【19†2024 Manifesto - Easy read (.pdf)†assets.nationbuilder.com】\nL25: \nL26: 【20†2024 Manifesto - Large print (.docx)†assets.nationbuilder.com】\nL27: \nL28: 2024 Manifesto - BSL interpretation:\nL29: \nL30: 【21†Maniffesto Plaid Cymru 2024 - BSL†cdn.embedly.com】\nL31: \nL32: 2024 Manifesto - Audio version:\nL33: \nL34: 【22†2024 Manifesto - Audio version†cdn.embedly.com】\nL35: \nL36: * * *\nL37: ### PCC Elections\nL38: \nL39: 【23†2024 PCC Manifesto (.pdf)†assets.nationbuilder.com】\nL40: \nL41: 【24†2024 PCC Manifesto - Easy read (.pdf)†assets.nationbuilder.com】\nL42: ## Sign up as a supporter!\nL43: \nL44: [Input][Input][Input]\nL45: \nL46: Optional email code\nL47: [Input]\nL48: \nL49: Email [Input]\nL50: \nL51: Post code [Input]\nL52: \nL53: Would you like to receive email updates?\nL54: \nL55: [Input] Yes (Recommended)\nL56: \nL57: [Input] No\nL58: \nL59: [Button: Sign up as a supporter!]\nL60: \nL61: 【25†Image†assets.nationbuilder.com】\nL62: \nL63:   * 【26†Privacy policy】\nL64:   * 【27†Unsubscribe】\nL65:   * 【5†Governance】\nL66:   * 【7†Contact】\nL67: \nL68: © 2025 Plaid Cymru - The Party of Wales\nL69: 【28†Promoted by Plaid Cymru, Tŷ Gwynfor, Cardiff, CF10 4AL】\nL70: Created by 【29†Brand Response†www.brandresponse.cc】 with 【30†NationBuilder†nationbuilder.com】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Wealth of Our Nation - Restore Britain (https://www.restorebritain.org.uk/the_wealth_of_our_nation)\nciteturn22view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.restorebritain.org.uk/the_wealth_of_our_nation\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 36\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2:   * 【1†Investigations】\nL3: \nL4: 【1†Investigations】 【2†Whistleblowing】 【3†FOI Investigations】\nL5: # The Wealth of Our Nation\nL6: \nL7: August 03, 2026\nL8: \nL9: Restore Britain has today published The Wealth of Our Nation, a paper diagnosing four decades of political choices behind Britain's economic decline, and setting out a costed path to reversing it.\nL10: Britain's GDP per head was once 8.9 times that of Poland. On current trends, Poland will overtake Britain within a decade. Some 246,000 British nationals left the country in the year to December 2025 alone, many of them young and skilled, even as the state has grown to swallow nearly half of the economy and taxation has reached its highest share of national income since 1948.\nL11: Restore Britain rejects the claim that public services are underfunded. The average British household now contributes £44,000 a year in tax to fund public services that most consider worse than a generation ago. Left unreformed, the paper warns, the working-age welfare bill alone will cost each household £14,500 a year in transfer payments by 2030.\nL12: The party's answer is to claw back £178 billion of the £300 billion in excess spending accumulated since 2019, roughly £35 billion a year, through a freeze on working-age benefits and QUANGO budgets, reform of the pensions triple lock, and the end of Net Zero-related public expenditure.\nL13: Every pound saved is earmarked to fund £155-156 billion of tax cuts, including a higher personal allowance, a restored 19% rate of corporation tax, and the abolition of inheritance tax, stamp duty, and insurance premium tax.\nL14: The party's ambition is a state no larger than the one Tony Blair inherited in 1997, roughly 33% of GDP against 45% today, achieved over two Parliaments.\nL15: \nL16: Read the paper in full 【4†here†assets.nationbuilder.com】.\nL17: \nL18: General Enquiries: 【5†[email protected]】\nL19: \nL20: Press Enquiries: 【6†[email protected]】\nL21: \nL22: 【7†Privacy Policy†assets.nationbuilder.com】\nL23: \nL24: Promoted by Restore Britain of Suite 4, Millennium House, Gapton Hall Road, Great Yarmouth, Norfolk, England, NR31 0NL\nL25: \nL26: * * *\nL27: ##### Restore Britain\nL28: \nL29: United Kingdom\nL30: \nL31: Created with 【8†NationBuilder†nationbuilder.com】\nL32: \nL33: The Wealth of our Nation\nL34: \nL35: The Wealth of Our Nation\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAbolish Inheritance Tax - Restore Britain (https://www.restorebritain.org.uk/policy_paper_abolish_inheritance_tax)\nciteturn22view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.restorebritain.org.uk/policy_paper_abolish_inheritance_tax\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 36\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2:   * 【1†Investigations】\nL3: \nL4: 【1†Investigations】 【2†Whistleblowing】 【3†FOI Investigations】\nL5: # Abolish Inheritance Tax\nL6: \nL7: March 17, 2026\nL8: \nL9: Restore Britain has today launched a policy document titled ‘Abolish Inheritance Tax. In our latest policy paper, Restore Britain sets out the case for abolishing inheritance tax in full.\nL10: The paper argues that inheritance tax is a de facto tax on death that violates the fundamental moral principle that families should be free to pass the fruits of a lifetime’s labour to their children. Human beings are social beings with deeply felt inter-generational bonds who work not only for themselves but for the good of our families, unborn as well as living. Taxing inheritance therefore weakens the link between generations and undermines the social fabric.\nL11: The policy paper highlights the particular damage inheritance tax does to family farms and small businesses, many of which are asset-rich but cash-poor. Recent government plans to extend inheritance tax to agricultural assets threaten to force families to sell land and businesses simply to pay tax bills when a relative dies, putting pressure on the countryside and the enterprises that sustain local communities.\nL12: The paper also notes that inheritance tax raises only around £9 billion per year — roughly 0.7% of total tax revenue — meaning it plays only a minor role in funding the state. Restore Britain argues that the revenue lost from abolishing the tax could easily be offset by reducing wasteful or ideological spending elsewhere in government.\nL13: The paper proposes cutting taxpayer-funded DEI roles, ending state funding for activist NGOs, and reforming charity law provisions that currently allow political organisations to receive public money and tax privileges.\nL14: \nL15: We conclude that abolishing inheritance tax would protect family farms, small businesses, and ordinary households, while ensuring that the wealth created by hard-working Britons can be passed on to their loved ones rather than confiscated by the state.\nL16: You can read the paper in full 【4†here†assets.nationbuilder.com】.\nL17: \nL18: General Enquiries: 【5†[email protected]】\nL19: \nL20: Press Enquiries: 【6†[email protected]】\nL21: \nL22: 【7†Privacy Policy†assets.nationbuilder.com】\nL23: \nL24: Promoted by Restore Britain of Suite 4, Millennium House, Gapton Hall Road, Great Yarmouth, Norfolk, England, NR31 0NL\nL25: \nL26: * * *\nL27: ##### Restore Britain\nL28: \nL29: United Kingdom\nL30: \nL31: Created with 【8†NationBuilder†nationbuilder.com】\nL32: \nL33: Abolish Inheritance Tax\nL34: \nL35: Abolish Inheritance Tax\n"
